.SS "int32_t schultz_window_create (const \fBschultz_window_options\fP * options, \fBschultz_window\fP ** out_window)"

.PP
Opens a window and builds everything drawing it needs\&. On success the tree is empty but ready: its viewport and root bounds match the window, its theme is the built in dark one, its font system, image table and clipboard are wired up, and an event router is attached\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIoptions\fP How to start\&. NULL accepts every default\&. 
.br
\fIout_window\fP Receives the window\&. Must not be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
SCHULTZ_OK, SCHULTZ_ERR_INVALID_ARGUMENT when out_window is NULL or the platform refused the window, or SCHULTZ_ERR_OUT_OF_MEMORY\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "const char * schultz_window_error (void)"

.PP
Returns the platform's description of the most recent failure\&. A result code says what went wrong in the toolkit's terms; when the window itself is what failed, this says why in the platform's\&. It is the only reason a host ever needs the platform layer, so it is passed through here rather than leaving that header to be included\&.
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A NUL terminated string owned by the platform\&. Never NULL, but it is empty when nothing has failed\&. 
.RE
.PP

